    "question": {
      ":question/id": "df542574-4e6e-5170-a3f5-bae1cab6f2ed",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sin\\left(126^\\circ\\right)}{\\sin\\left(63^\\circ\\right)}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $s=\\sin\\left(63^\\circ\\right)$ and $c=\\cos\\left(63^\\circ\\right)$. The **double-angle formula** gives $\\sin\\left(126^\\circ\\right)=2sc$.\n\n\n\nExpand the doubled sine and cancel the common factor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2sc}{s} &=2c \\\\ &=2\\cos\\left(63^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll cancellations use nonzero factors in the original expression.",
